Article 28 The State export control authorities shall, according to law, supervise and inspect the export activities of controlled items.
Where the State export control authorities investigate an act suspected of violating the provisions of this Law, they may take the following measures:
(1) Entering the business premises or other relevant premises of the person under investigation for inspection;
(2) Inquiring of the person under investigation, interested parties, and other relevant organizations or individuals, and requiring them to provide explanations on matters related to the incident under investigation;
(3) Consulting and copying relevant documents and materials such as documents, agreements, accounting books, and business correspondence of the person under investigation, interested parties, and other relevant organizations or individuals;
(4) Inspecting means of transport used for export, preventing the loading of suspected export items, and ordering the return of illegally exported items;
(5) Sealing up or seizing the relevant items involved;
(6) Inquiring into the bank accounts of the person under investigation.
The measures under subparagraphs (5) and (6) of the preceding paragraph shall be taken only with the written approval of the head of the State export control authorities.

Article 34 Where an export operator commits any of the following acts, the illegal act shall be ordered to cease, the illegal gains shall be confiscated, and if the illegal turnover is 500,000 RMB or more, a fine of not less than five times but not more than ten times the illegal turnover shall also be imposed; if there is no illegal turnover or the illegal turnover is less than 500,000 RMB, a fine of not less than 500,000 RMB but not more than 5,000,000 RMB shall also be imposed; if the circumstances are serious, the operator shall be ordered to suspend business for rectification, until the relevant export operation qualification for controlled items is revoked:
(1) Exporting controlled items without permission;
(2) Exporting controlled items beyond the scope of permission specified in the export license;
(3) Exporting controlled items whose export is prohibited.
